  "contribution": {
    "summary": "Qualify a new dw.quantities.standard calendar-version NuGet candidate with exact pinned dependencies on both independently published Math packages and ten binary-only consumer checks.",
    "value": "Link five unchanged Standard sources in a temporary packaging project, use shared NuGet F1 version and package reader, confirm exact nuspec dependency closure, three DLL SHA-256 values, 250 g = 1/4 kg and explicit ambiguity handling.",
    "debtChanges": [
      "The historical Standard source package stays at 0.2.0-preview.1 with two ProjectReference edges; only a disposable packaging projection substitutes exact PackageReferences.",
      "RS141 creates an unreserved, unpublished calendar candidate; immutable NUGET_LOCAL publication and independently qualified readback require later separate gates.",
      "Public licensing, package notices, installed-package rollback, other OS/RID platforms and Discovery/Decision integration remain outside the qualification.",
      "The RS140 predecessor succeeded at allocated attempt 001 after one pre-attempt refusal; its run-level first-pass is NO, and historical publication receipts are retained unchanged."
    ],
    "nextAction": "After RS141 succeeds, examine the dynamic Standard candidate and two exact source-independent dependency DLL hashes; qualify a disposable shared NuGet publisher rehearsal before separately authorized local publication and DWF readback.",
